MamaRetrieval — Research-Only License v1
========================================

This dataset ("the Dataset") is released by the maintainer
(see the dataset card / README.md) for non-commercial academic research
and retrieval-evaluation benchmarking only. By downloading, accessing,
copying, or using the Dataset, in whole or in part, you agree to the
following terms.

1. Permitted use
----------------
The following uses are permitted without further written permission:

  (a) Academic research, including publication of aggregate metrics,
      qualitative analysis, ablations, error analysis, and methodology
      comparisons.
  (b) Use of the Dataset as an evaluation benchmark for retrieval
      systems, including running new retrievers or alternative judges
      against the included (query, chunk) pairs.
  (c) Use of the rubric, prompts, manifest, and structured metadata
      for methodology research.

2. Prohibited use
-----------------
The following are prohibited without explicit written permission from
the maintainer:

  (a) Any commercial use, including but not limited to evaluation as
      part of internal product decisions at for-profit organisations,
      paid consulting deliverables, or commercial publications.
  (b) Use of the chunk text contained in chunks.parquet as training
      data for any model — generative, embedding, retrieval,
      classification, or otherwise — at any stage of training,
      fine-tuning, or instruction-tuning.
  (c) Redistribution of the chunk text, in whole or in part, outside
      the form shipped in this Dataset. This includes extracting
      chunks.parquet, repackaging the content into another dataset,
      mirroring, or re-hosting.
  (d) Production deployment of any system whose retrieval, ranking,
      or judging behaviour has been tuned, calibrated, or otherwise
      adapted using the Dataset.
  (e) Clinical use of the chunk text. The chunk content has NOT been
      reviewed for clinical accuracy in the form presented here. Do
      not surface chunk text to patients, clinicians, or any
      end-user clinical workflow.

3. Upstream licensing
---------------------
The chunk text was assembled from a corpus that mixes open-licensed
sources (some under variants of CC BY-NC-SA) with closed-licensed
clinical references. This License does NOT relicense or grant any
rights over the underlying upstream content beyond the research-use
scope set out in Section 1. Where a use case is not strictly
research evaluation under Section 1, independent verification of
upstream licensing for each chunk source is the user's responsibility.

4. No warranty
--------------
The Dataset is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind,
express or implied. The maintainer makes no representations about
the clinical accuracy, completeness, currency, or suitability of the
chunk text or the LLM-generated judgments for any purpose.

5. Attribution
--------------
Any publication or public use under Section 1 must cite the Dataset
as indicated in the Citation section of the dataset card.

6. Contact
----------
If your intended use does not fit cleanly within Section 1, contact
the maintainer (see dataset card) before proceeding.
